# Every .sql file in this repo is generated/authored as pure LF and is
# expected to stay byte-for-byte identical regardless of which OS checks it
# out — tests/wholesaleSeedSql.test.js (and the SQL migration test files
# next to it) compare a committed .sql file's exact bytes against a
# generator function's in-memory output, which always produces "\n" only.
# Without this file, a Windows checkout with the machine-wide Git for
# Windows default (core.autocrlf=true) silently rewrites every .sql file to
# CRLF on disk, which fails that comparison — not because the SQL content
# actually drifted, but because of a platform-specific checkout artifact.
# `eol=lf` pins the checked-out line ending to LF on every platform,
# independent of the developer's own core.autocrlf setting.
*.sql text eol=lf
